# Jungle model style (mesh craft)

Workflow: finish each prop as its own hero object first. Do not mass-generate or assemble the full map until individual assets are approved.

## Silhouette & form

- Faceted, but not primitive — keep large readable planes.
- Silhouettes smoother than stock low-poly Cube / Icosphere / Cone.
- Primary + secondary + tertiary forms on every tree, rock, and plant.
- Slight asymmetry; no perfect symmetry.
- Detail must read from `MAIN_GAME_CAMERA`. No invisible micro-detail.

## Forbidden

- Do not ship unedited Cube, Icosphere, or Cone as final meshes.
- No photoreal scans, noisy subdivision, or tiny bevel chatter.

## Mesh finish (default for most objects)

- Bevel Modifier: 2–3 segments.
- Bevel width ≈ 0.5–2% of object size (edges catch light).
- Shade Smooth by Angle (or current Blender Auto Smooth equivalent).
- Weighted Normal when it improves the result.
- Controlled poly counts (medium-poly, not extreme low-poly).

## Surface & grounding

- Mild color gradient (height or facing).
- Distinct light and dark planes — not a flat single shade.
- Correct ground contact: trunks reach terrain; rocks partially embedded; plants follow normals.

## Validation before approval

- Readable silhouette from `MAIN_GAME_CAMERA`.
- Bevels catch light on edges.
- No floating contact.
- Viewport screenshot + camera render of the single object (or small kit review).
